# What never belongs in the repository.
#
# Two kinds of thing are listed here. Build output, which is regenerated by
# BUILD.bat or by the workflow and is large. And a commander's own data,
# which is the more important half: settings.json holds an Inara API key,
# and deposits.csv is somebody's survey. Neither is ours to publish.

# ---- build output -------------------------------------------------------
# Anchored to the root on purpose. build/ itself is source - installer.iss,
# the PyInstaller specs, bump.py and site.py all live there - and only
# PyInstaller's scratch tree inside it is disposable.
/dist/
/upload/
build/work/

# ---- Python -------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# RUN.bat makes .venv; BUILD.bat makes .venv-build.
.venv/
.venv-build/
env/
venv/

# ---- a commander's own data ---------------------------------------------
# These live in %LOCALAPPDATA%\RadioRaxxla\EDSMT on an installed build, but
# running from source in a clone writes them next to the code.
settings.json
deposits.csv
locations.csv
crash.log
journal-mining-events.log
portable.txt
settings.json.bak
settings-history/
sessions.csv
rigs.json
imported.json
# With portable.txt beside the code, the data goes in data\ instead.
/data/

# ---- databases and secrets ----------------------------------------------
# The community API is run by Radio Raxxla and its source is not part of
# this project. None of these belong in it either.
/server/
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
.env
.env.*

# ---- anything captured from the game ------------------------------------
# Handy to have locally while chasing a reader bug, never to be committed:
# a journal names the commander on every line.
Status.json
Market.json
Cargo.json
Journal.*.log

# ---- editors and operating systems --------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Maintainer notes kept beside the project. Never committed; the names are
# listed so a copy left here by mistake cannot slip in.
internal/
RUNBOOK.md
DEVLOG.md
DECISIONS.md
BACKLOG.md
UPDATE-GUIDE.md
LEAK-TERMS.txt
